== Summary

Once artifact-gate 0.1.1 is on crates.io, this repo still pins 0.1.0 and still spells "no subsections" as `forbid` over a wildcard path pair, the workaround the upstream change exists to retire.


== Scope

Bump `artifact-gate` to `0.1.1` in `crates/mindtape/Cargo.toml` and `Cargo.lock`. If mindtape's own compile of `allowed` in `crates/mindtape/src/gate.rs` refuses an empty list before artifact-gate sees it, lift that as well, with a red test. Then replace the subsection rule in `.mindtape/config.toml`, keeping its message and rewriting the comment above it that points at the upstream refusal:

```toml
[[tasks.body.headers.rules]]
action = "allowlist"
scope = [{ match = ".*" }]
allowed = []
when = "!terminal"
message = "sections take no subsections; if a section needs one, the task is too big"
```

Add a CHANGELOG.md entry saying a project config may now declare an empty allowlist. The crate version facts the docs read are regenerated by the docs gate, never by hand.


== Dogfood

Built in: the allowlist form becomes this repo's own subsection rule.

